// The size class of a request: classes start at class pc_c with blocks of pc_z
// bytes (or cells) and each doubles the one before. Lists start at class 1 with
// four cells and strings at class 36 with sixteen bytes, so one loop serves both
// (more/pool.id has the heads).

pool_cls(word pc_z, word pc_c, word pc_t) {
  while(pc_z < pc_t) {
    pc_z = pc_z * 2;
    pc_c = pc_c + 1;
  }
} return word pc_c;
(16, 36, 16):(36)
(16, 36, 17):(37)
(16, 36, 32):(37)
(16, 36, 33):(38)
(4, 1, 4):(1)
(4, 1, 5):(2)
